  "methods": [
    "USGS MRDS WFS points inside the district polygon (point-in-polygon, EPSG:4326)",
    "exactextract coverage weight area_spherical_km2 at 3 arc-seconds (about 90 m); slope from central differences with latitude-dependent metres per degree; missing ocean tiles are no data",
    "exactextract class fractions, coverage weight area_spherical_km2, read at 40 m (overview read, factor 4, nearest); share of mapped area inside the district polygon",
    "exactextract coverage weight area_spherical_km2 at 1 arc-second (about 30 m); land pixels (datamask = 1) only; forest = treecover2000 >= 30%; loss counted inside 2000 forest by lossyear",
    "ISRIC WCS 2.0.1 GetCoverage on the native 250 m Homolosine grid (request bounds snapped to the grid, no resampling); cells the service returns as 0 (SoilGrids mask: built-up, water, rock) and their uncertainty cells treated as no data; district polygons reprojected to Homolosine; exactextract coverage-weighted (area_cartesian); values divided by the ISRIC conversion factor",
    "exactextract class fractions, coverage weight area_spherical_km2, on the 0.5 degree GLiM grid; coarse: a district usually spans a few cells",
    "exactextract coverage weight area_spherical_km2 on the native 0.05 degree grid; negative values treated as no data; normals are the mean of yearly district means",
    "Theil-Sen slope (median of the slopes between every pair of years) of the yearly district means, times ten for a decade; two-sided Mann-Kendall test, normal approximation with the tie-corrected variance and continuity correction; written only for a complete series of at least 30 years",
    "annual mean of the twelve monthly means of each 0.5 degree cell, a cell missing any month left out of that year; Kelvin less 273.15; exactextract coverage weight area_spherical_km2 on the native grid; normals are the mean of yearly district means",
    "Averaged over each district on the 1 km grid, each cell weighted by the share of it inside the district; the 10th and 90th percentiles are across the district's cells",
    "River reaches measured inside each district; a major river carries at least 100 m³/s on average; distance from the district's centre to the nearest major river"
  ],
